;; The import system as importlib._bootstrap (PY6b, PYS12 (a)): as CPython's pylifecycle.c does it, the stdlib's
;; Lib/importlib/_bootstrap.py runs as the frozen module _frozen_importlib, _bootstrap._install(sys, _imp)
;; puts BuiltinImporter and FrozenImporter on sys.meta_path, Lib/importlib/_bootstrap_external.py runs as
;; _frozen_importlib_external, _bootstrap._install_external_importers() adds PathFinder and FileFinder's path
;; hook, and zipimport.zipimporter goes first among the path hooks. It is installed at an interpreter's first
;; import that sys.modules does not answer; from then on an import that sys.modules does not answer is
;; _bootstrap._find_and_load(name, __import__) (import.go keeps CPython's C part: sys.modules, the relative
;; names, the fromlist), and the runtime's own finder (import.go's findAndLoad) is left for an interpreter
;; whose search path holds no Lib/importlib. The frozen modules are CPython 3.14's list (Python/frozen.c),
;; each the code of its Lib/ source compiled under the name "<frozen ORIGNAME>", as CPython's freeze tool
;; names it; __hello_only__ (Tools/freeze/flag.py, outside Lib/) is not among them.

